  "result": "Perfect! All implementations are complete and working correctly. Here's the final summary:\n\n## Summary: Late Fees Report Function\n\nI've successfully added the `lateFee` function to the `src/reports.js` module:\n\n### Implementation: `lateFee(invoice, asOf)`\n\nThe function calculates late fees based on:\n- **Rate**: 0.04% per day overdue (of the amount still due)\n- **Eligibility**: Only for invoices with status `issued` or `partially_paid`\n- **Calculation**: `fee = due \u00d7 (daysOverdue \u00d7 0.04 / 100)`\n- **Returns**: Fee in cents (rounded), or 0 if not overdue\n\nKey features:\n- Returns 0 for draft, paid, or null invoices\n- Returns 0 for invoices not yet due\n- Handles partially paid invoices (uses remaining balance)\n- Properly rounds fees using banker's rounding via `roundCents`\n- Accounts for all invoice modifications (discounts, vouchers, VAT-exempt items)\n\n### Test Coverage: 24 comprehensive test cases\n\nTests verify:\n- Status filtering (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- Due date comparisons (before, on, after due date)\n- Single and multiple days overdue\n- Fully unpaid and partially paid invoices\n- Various invoice types (discounted, VAT-exempt, tier-discounted)\n- Rounding behavior\n- Edge cases (null invoices, future dates, year/month boundaries)\n- Data immutability\n\n**Final Test Results: 367/367 passing**\n- 318 original tests\n- 25 vatSummary tests  \n- 24 lateFee tests\n\nThe late fee calculation correctly compounds over time: 1 day overdue incurs a 0.04% fee, 10 days incurs 0.4%, 30 days incurs 1.2%, etc.",
